            "review_title": "Review at Bedori Halal Restaurant in Ho Chi Minh City",
            "review_text": "Audrey E\nBerwick, Australia345 contributions\n0\nVery good food hidden down an alley\nOct 2026 • Solo\nI was the only person in the restaurant for lunch and I shouldn't have picked the table facing the kitchen since the 2 men there (server and another man) were sitting right in front of me, one facing me, which felt a little awkward. Despite this, the food was delicious. A very good paratha which is often badly done. Very generous serves of both curry and rice, so much so I couldn't finish it. A good mango lassi too. Just watch out for the bottle of water. This was brought to my table when I sat down. I wasn't asked if I wanted it so presumed it was complimentary but they charged me for it, so refuse it if you don't want to pay for it.\nRead more\nWritten October 8, 2026",
